  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Administration and economic justice programme support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Economic Justice Programme focuses primarily on the issues of Debt, Social Rights and the Social Securirty System. Special attention is given to defending the social rights contained within the Brazilian Constitution, combating electoral corruption, carrying out the social audits of the debt and building leadership capacity in social movements across Brazil and Latin America.

The programme is implemented by CAFOD and four Brazilian partners experienced in education, campaigning and advocacy and with strong Church links. The implementing organisations include the Social Comission (Pastoral Social) of the Bishops&apos; Conference, the Justice and Peace Comission, Jubilee South/Brazil and the Cry of the Excluded.

A first meeting took place between CAFOD and these partners in 2003 with a view towards strengthening networking and facilitating lesson sharing. Further partner meetings were held in 2004, 2005 and 2006 with the issue of debt and social rights identified by partners as the basis for collective campaigning and advocacy work in the coming three years, 2007-2009. The Economic Justice Programme follows on from the church programme (2004-2006) which involved the same partners.</narrative>
  </description>
